WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.280
I was accused last
weekend, I, I don't know,

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.060
this is up to the listener to decide;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.350
but I was accused by my
compatriots, the chilled chums,

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.980
of not being very chill and, and,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.980
and being sort of ratcheted
up and coming in hot.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.740
And that may be the case. I don't know.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.545
I'm, I'm humble enough
to accept that I am,

00:00:24.545 --> 00:00:28.720
despite incredible powers (Matt chuckles)

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.719
I am-

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.552
[Sona] Oh my God.

00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:31.970
A human and flawed.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.020
And so it's possible that
I was not chill last week,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.410
and if that's the case, I'm sorry

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.450
and I will to try to be more chill.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.300
[Sona] Hmm.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.660
During this episode,
I'll do the best I can.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.033
So, with that in mind, let's, let's begin.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.110
Sona, it's nice to have you on the show.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.793
It's very nice to be here.

00:00:55.811 --> 00:00:57.715
But you don't, yeah. Okay. You seem okay.

00:00:57.715 --> 00:01:00.040
(All laugh)

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.880
I don't wanna, we were just talking

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.610
about murder in the summer.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:08.060
And so I realized that's not a
very chill topic to bring up.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.435
So, I have nothing to say right now.

00:01:10.435 --> 00:01:11.268
[Conan] Well, let me explain.

00:01:11.268 --> 00:01:13.930
Because all I have in
my mind is murder. Okay.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.050
Before we came on the air. On the air,

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.930
before we pressed record,
whatever is the correct term,

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.447
Matt, what's the correct term?

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:22.938
I think press record. But you know-

00:01:22.938 --> 00:01:23.771
[Sona] Started recording

00:01:23.771 --> 00:01:24.604
it's a general term.

00:01:24.604 --> 00:01:26.070
I think people would forgive you for that.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.080
Okay. I don't understand
the podcast format.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.040
I actually still don't
understand television

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.865
after doing it for 27
years. So you'll forgive me

00:01:35.865 --> 00:01:38.630
if I, if I'm a little
clumsy in my wording,

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.630
but the point we were, before
we started this episode,

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.050
we were all just chatting;
and of course, I would say

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.650
the one thing the three of
us really have in common

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.370
is, maybe a lot of people have this,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.199
but we all are very obsessed with murder.

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:56.032
(Sona agrees)

00:01:56.032 --> 00:02:00.660
I love, and, I don't love murder,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.763
I mean, that's a terrible thing to say.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.771
Yes, in a perfect world,
I would be able to murder.

00:02:06.771 --> 00:02:08.790
What? What? (Matt laughs)

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.030
But I understand that there
are social conventions

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.050
and laws, and I, I don't
want to go to prison

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.075
so I will not murder.

00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:15.908
What a-

00:02:15.908 --> 00:02:16.741
[Conan] Despite my -

00:02:16.741 --> 00:02:18.139
What a sick thing to say. Okay.

00:02:18.139 --> 00:02:20.100
Despite my insatiable desire for murder

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.968
(Sona laughs loudly)

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.550
and the constant voice in my head

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.320
that says, "Murder, murder,
you know it's what you want,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.863
you know it's what you're good at."

00:02:27.863 --> 00:02:28.696
(Sona laughs)

00:02:28.696 --> 00:02:29.930
[Matt] Sometimes that's not
just in your head by the way,

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.720
that you say that out loud.
(Sona continues laughing)

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.597
By the way, I'm saying this,
I think in a very chill way.

00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:38.500
You did come in fairly chill this episode,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.359
I want to say, you didn't come in hot.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.871
[Conan] And you know what?
My tone is still very chill.

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:43.704
(Sona laughs)

00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:45.580
As I tell you, (Matt laughs) my greatest,

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:50.580
my greatest desire in life
is to, to wantonly murder,

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.590
rob other people of their
lives and get away with it.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:55.657
[Sona] Oh my God! (laughing)

00:02:55.657 --> 00:02:58.830
But there you go. That's,
and I'm just saying that

00:02:58.830 --> 00:02:59.830
as a chill chum.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:00.769
Yeah.

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:03.600
[Sona] Before you even said
that, if you did murder

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.967
and someone came up to me and said,

00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:06.950
"Hey, did you ever think
he'd be the kind of guy

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.714
who'd murder?" I'd be
like, "Yes, absolutely".

00:03:09.714 --> 00:03:10.547
Yeah

00:03:10.547 --> 00:03:11.930
[Sona] He talks about murder all the time.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.636
I'm obsessed with murder.

00:03:13.636 --> 00:03:14.469
[Sona] Yeah!

00:03:14.469 --> 00:03:18.460
And what is interesting
is that, Sona, you know,

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.887
I hired Sona. We all do
things we later regret,

00:03:22.887 --> 00:03:25.037
but I did hire Sona
(Conan and Matt laugh).

00:03:26.312 --> 00:03:27.145
[Sona] That's unnecessary.

00:03:27.145 --> 00:03:29.355
No, I'm kidding, I'm kidding. I'm kidding.

00:03:29.355 --> 00:03:30.188
Unnecessary, terrible.

00:03:30.188 --> 00:03:31.354
Unnecessary. Terrible.

00:03:31.354 --> 00:03:34.970
I love you Sona, but I did
hire you, and one of the things

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.450
we did early on because I'd
just moved out to Los Angeles,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.960
this is like 11 years ago,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.800
we'd just moved out to Los Angeles,

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.750
Sona and I were, I think we were somewhere

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.960
in the car together cause
we had to do something.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.960
And you said, "Oh wait, this
is near the, the, you know,

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:55.160
the scene of the first Manson murders."

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.930
You know, the, on Cielo Drive.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.850
Well, we were on Benedict
Canyon, which is -

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.390
Benedict Canyon. And then the two of us

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.223
were immediately like,

00:04:01.223 --> 00:04:02.240
"Oh, we've got to go up there and see it",

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.860
which I know sounds ghastly
and, and, and everything.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:10.490
But we were both, we both
knew every single detail

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:15.470
of, you know, Manson and
the whole history of Manson.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.400
And that's when we realized,
okay this is something

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.670
we have in common. We have
many things that we're,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:25.230
that we aren't in common,
where we were not alike.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.830
I could go on at length about those.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.360
[Sona] Nope. Move on. Okay. Yeah.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.890
I cherish America.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.360
Oh, wow!

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.390
[Matt] Geez.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.223
Okay

00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:38.222
I, whatever. But-

00:04:38.222 --> 00:04:40.850
You were telling a nice
story about us looking

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.460
at the house where, you know-

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.720
Yeah, what a nice story!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.782
[Sona] What a nice story
about driving. (Matt laughs)

00:04:45.782 --> 00:04:49.030
What a nice tale! Of us
retracing, retracing the steps.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.760
But we knew all the people
in the car, we knew then,

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.610
you know, about what
they did the next night.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.860
We knew, we knew everything;
and then I realized

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.940
that whenever I'm traveling
or going anywhere,

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.740
the first thing I try and
look for is the forensic files

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.280
because they show one after
another, after another,

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.807
after another; and I just watch those.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.550
[Sona] Uh huh.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.500
And I'm fascinated with that stuff.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.710
And Matt, you have some
interest in murder?

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.320
Yeah, I suppose I grew up in the place

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.510
where the night stalker did his
nights stalking in Whittier.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:24.180
And so it was really kind
of big in the community

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.790
obviously at the time.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.373
Right. That was a big story-

00:05:27.373 --> 00:05:28.206
[Matt] Yeah.

00:05:28.206 --> 00:05:29.039
That was a big thing. Yeah.

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:31.920
And my wife was in a play with a guy

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.270
who did a double murder
and dismembered the bodies

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.570
and spread them throughout a park.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.679
Oh, my God!

00:05:37.679 --> 00:05:39.080
[Conan] Wait, what?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.430
[Sona] This is not chill.

